1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,480
Number 13 lightweight gear isn't always the best.
第十三点：轻量装备并不总是最好的选择。

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:08,200
So when I bought my first round of wild camping gear it was great.
刚买第一批野外露营装备时，我觉得挺好。

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:16,880
But then I went down the rabbit hole of buying gear that was lighter and lighter and lighter just to try and take a little bit of weight off my back.
但后来我越陷越深，不断买更轻、更轻的装备，只为减轻背部一点负重。

4
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:21,840
Um I should have taken a bit more weight off my front which would have made things a lot easier.
他自嘲说，当时更该减掉一点自己肚子前面的重量，那样事情会轻松得多。

5
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:31,320
But you know at some point you are sacrificing or I found that you're sacrificing comfort just to save a little bit of weight.
但到了某个程度，他发现为了省下一点重量，牺牲的却是舒适感。

6
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:36,840
I'd rather carry a little bit more on me back but have a good night's sleep.
我宁愿背上多一点东西，也想睡一个好觉。

7
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:43,600
So I've tried sleeping on sleeping pads that are literally millimeters thick.
我试过睡在真的只有几毫米厚的睡垫上。

8
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:46,629
And I just don't sleep at all so what is the point.
结果我根本睡不着，那还有什么意义呢？

9
00:00:46,639 --> 00:00:54,920
I may as well carry a sleepy self inflating pad that can maybe 400 gram but have a good night's sleep.
他觉得还不如带一张约400克的自充气垫，换来一夜好眠。

10
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:59,320
So it's all about striking a balance between comfort and weight.
所以关键就是在舒适和重量之间找到平衡。

11
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:09,000
So I started at this level started going for the lighter weight stuff and as I got older I want wanted comfort more so for me comfort is king every time.
他起初用普通装备，后来追求轻量；随着年龄增长又更想舒适，所以对他来说，舒适总是第一位。

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,200
You've got to find out what works for you one thing I will say though is is don't pack your fears.
你得找到适合自己的方式。不过他还想说一点：别把自己的担心全装进背包。

13
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:24,880
So don't pack a spare stove just in case one breaks don't take two sleeping bags just in case one's not going to be quite warm enough.
他举例说，不要只因怕炉具坏了就带备用炉具，也不要只因怕不够暖就带两个睡袋。

14
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:32,639
You know don't take four spare t shirts in case you get wet three times it's you don't need all of that gear.
也不要因为担心湿三次，就带四件备用T恤。他觉得不需要那么多装备。

15
00:01:32,639 --> 00:01:38,880
If you start packing for everything you think might go wrong you'll end up taking a trailer with you.
如果把所有可能出错的情况都考虑进去装包，最后就得拖个拖车了。

16
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:42,519
Number 14 don't be afraid to abandon ship.
第十四点：别害怕中途放弃。

17
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:48,279
If things are rotten you're having a terrible night the wind is blowing you all over the place.
如果情况很糟、晚上过得很不舒服，风又把人吹得东倒西歪。

18
00:01:48,279 --> 00:01:53,480
There is no shame in just packing up and going home you've got nothing to prove to anybody.
收拾回家没什么丢人的，你不需要向任何人证明什么。

19
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:59,920
I used to quite enjoy challenging myself and you know seeing how I could cope in really testing conditions.
过去我挺喜欢挑战自己，看看能在多么考验人的环境里应付下来。

20
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:08,080
But the older I get maybe a little bit wiser while camp for me about the enjoyment of it I want to be able to soak up the views.
但随着年纪增长，也许更明智了，他露营更看重享受，想好好欣赏风景。

21
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:14,080
I want to be able to chill out and relax and sort of bond with nature a little bit I don't want to be fighting it.
我想放松休息，和自然有一点联结，不想与它较劲。

22
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:18,279
I don't want to be holding on to a trekking pole all night trying to keep my tent up.
我不想整夜抓着登山杖，只为撑住自己的帐篷。

23
00:02:18,279 --> 00:02:23,279
There's been quite a few times when I've pulled up to the car park where I'm just about to go wild camping.
有好几次，我开车到了停车场，正准备出发去野外露营。

24
00:02:23,279 --> 00:02:29,279
And it is belting it down with rain and I've thought you know what there is always another day.
结果雨下得非常大，我就想：算了，总还有下一次。

25
00:02:29,279 --> 00:02:35,680
So I've driven home and just saved it for for an opportunity or a time when I'm going to enjoy it more.
于是我就开车回家，把行程留给更能享受它的机会或时候。

26
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:40,840
Don't get me wrong I do like to have a little bit of wind blowing through my hair every now and again.
别误会，我也喜欢偶尔让风吹吹头发。

27
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:46,470
But I don't want that to detract from the experience of wild camping.
但我不希望那影响野外露营本身的体验。

28
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:58,399
Number 15 respect the environment anybody that's looked into any sort of camping or while camping before must have heard the phrase leave no trace.
第十五点：尊重环境。研究过露营或野外露营的人，应该都听过“不留痕迹”这个说法。

29
00:02:58,399 --> 00:03:03,759
So you know when you've packed up and gone in the morning after you've had a night on the hills.
也就是说，在山里住了一晚、早晨收拾离开时。

30
00:03:03,759 --> 00:03:12,080
Make sure that the area that you've been in is clean tidy exactly how you found them in some cases better than how you found them.
确保待过的区域干净整洁，和刚来时一样，有时甚至比刚来时更好。

31
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:21,480
So if there's if you find a bit of rubbish that is not yours but you can put it in your rubbish bag do so and help clean things up a little bit.
所以，如果看到不是自己的垃圾，但能装进垃圾袋，就带上，也算帮忙清理一点。

32
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:30,500
When you think about it we're just guests on this planet for 70 or 80 years for most of us all of us are responsible for protecting and looking after the place.
仔细想想，我们多数人只是这颗星球上住七八十年的客人；每个人都有责任保护、照顾这里。
